  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Diphenadione is a vitamin K antagonist, a class of drugs used as antithrombotic (anticoagulant) agents to prevent blood clotting. It appears to be only an experimental compound today, with no marketing authorisation in the European Union, so it is not in routine human medical use.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q419386&quot;>Wikidata Q419386</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>diphenadione</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>B01AA10</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB13347&quot;>DB13347</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/6719&quot;>6719</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:81896&quot;>81896</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q419386&quot;>Q419386</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C23H16O3</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>340.378 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
